course: dictionary
lesson: 6173
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word «mink» is a good example. It can be an animal, or the soft fur that comes from it.
explain: In «American mink that escaped from fur farms hunt them in their burrows», the words hunt, burrows and escaped tell you mink is the animal. In «a mink coat», the word coat tells you mink means the fur, not the animal, because a coat is made from fur.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it. Swap in the animal, or swap in the fur, and see which one still makes sense. This check works for every word with more than one meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word.
fact: «Mink» can mean a small, thin animal of the weasel family, with dark brown fur.
fact: «Mink» can also mean its soft, shiny fur, or a coat made from that fur.
fact: The American mink escaped from fur farms in Britain and Ireland, and now hunts water voles and birds, which is a problem for river wildlife.
exercise: In «a mink coat», what does mink mean? | An animal that lives near rivers | A kind of boat | A small bird | *The soft, shiny fur, made into a coat
exercise: The mink is a member of which family? | Cat family | Bird family | Rat family | *Weasel family
exercise: In «American mink that escaped from fur farms hunt them in their burrows», what do the mink hunt? | *Water voles | Coats | Trees | Castles
test: Why are American mink a problem for river wildlife? | Because they sing loudly at night | Because they make expensive coats | Because they build dams on rivers | *Because they hunt water voles and birds
test: Which animal is from the same family as the mink? | Squirrel | *Stoat | Hedgehog | Mole
exam: In «a mink coat», which word tells you that mink means fur, not an animal? | *Coat | Soft | Brown | Hunting
